WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:03.520
BILL B.: One thing I can tell you is that the story I'm

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.000
gonna tell

00:00:05.019 --> 00:00:08.269
today is a kind of story you're not gonna hear from any

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.719
other speaker

00:00:07.719 --> 00:00:11.169
coming to this room at any other point.

00:00:11.189 --> 00:00:14.349
Will the me start out by telling you a little bit about

00:00:14.369 --> 00:00:17.050
myself.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.169
I was here at Stanford 20 years ago.

00:00:19.189 --> 00:00:22.829
I'm actually back for my 20-year reunion which is what

00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:23.849
brought me here

00:00:23.849 --> 00:00:24.849
today.

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:27.570
And so I thought maybe I would share with you a little bit

00:00:27.589 --> 00:00:28.589
of my own

00:00:28.589 --> 00:00:34.799
psychology when I was sitting in these seats 20 years ago.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.419
Probably when you hear me speaking, one of the questions

00:00:38.439 --> 00:00:39.569
that would

00:00:39.589 --> 00:00:42.839
show up in your mind is: What is this guy with an American

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:43.820
accent

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.529
from Chicago doing having been the -- at one point the

00:00:46.549 --> 00:00:47.549
largest foreign

00:00:47.549 --> 00:00:49.889
portfolio investor in Russia,

00:00:49.909 --> 00:00:53.409
and, what I will describe to you in a minute, now one of the

00:00:52.859 --> 00:00:53.859
biggest

00:00:53.859 --> 00:00:55.359
enemies of the State of Russia?

00:00:55.359 --> 00:01:00.869
And so let me explain to you how that all happened.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:02.179
Indeed I am an American.

00:01:02.199 --> 00:01:04.180
I'm from Chicago.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.730
But I come from a very unusual family.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:10.780
My grandfather who was also American, his name is Earl

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:11.829
Browder, grew

00:01:11.849 --> 00:01:13.310
up in Wichita, Kansas.

00:01:13.329 --> 00:01:18.620
And the family lost its farm, the home on the farm in the

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.709
1920s and he

00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:22.049
had to work in a factory.

00:01:22.069 --> 00:01:24.760
And the factory was mistreating their workers and so he

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:25.780
became a labor

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.890
union organizer and he was very good at it.

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:33.099
And so after working in Wichita he was recruited by the

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:34.119
Union to work

00:01:34.119 --> 00:01:37.619
in Kansas City then to work in New York City and in New York

00:01:37.469 --> 00:01:38.469
City

00:01:38.469 --> 00:01:40.769
there were various Communists that were running around and

00:01:40.789 --> 00:01:41.789
the

00:01:41.789 --> 00:01:44.620
Communists spotted him and said, this is a talented guy.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.140
Let's invite him to Moscow.

00:01:46.109 --> 00:01:49.109
And so the Communist Party invited him to Moscow in is the

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:49.939
27, he

00:01:49.959 --> 00:01:55.109
moved to Moscow there, he met my grandmother in Moscow, and

00:01:55.129 --> 00:01:56.129
my father

00:01:56.129 --> 00:01:57.129
was born there.

00:01:57.089 --> 00:02:00.590
And hen in 1942 he was sent back by the Communist Party to

00:02:00.609 --> 00:02:01.609
America to

00:02:01.609 --> 00:02:04.109
become the General secretary and head of the Communist Party

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:04.640
in

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.140
America for the next 13 years.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:06.359
&gt;&gt;

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.359
[Laughing]

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:11.259
BILL B.: This is my grandfather.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:11.479
&gt;&gt;

00:02:11.479 --> 00:02:12.479
[Laughing]

00:02:11.479 --> 00:02:17.569
BILL B.: The McCarthy era came in the is the 50s and I'm

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:18.639
sure you all

00:02:18.659 --> 00:02:22.159
know about that and so it wasn't such an easy time -- he got

00:02:21.509 --> 00:02:22.509
kicked

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:23.759
out of the Communist party.

00:02:23.759 --> 00:02:26.009
I should my grandfather 1945 for proposing that Communism

00:02:25.659 --> 00:02:26.659
and

00:02:26.659 --> 00:02:30.519
Capitalism could co-exist and unfortunately many of his

00:02:30.539 --> 00:02:31.539
followers in

00:02:31.539 --> 00:02:33.809
eastern Europe was assassinated.

00:02:33.829 --> 00:02:38.499
He was fortunate, living in America, that he wasn't.

00:02:38.519 --> 00:02:41.269
And then he was persecuted by McCarthy and had a very

00:02:40.759 --> 00:02:41.759
terrible time

00:02:41.759 --> 00:02:44.509
even after being kicked out of the Communist party in the

00:02:44.159 --> 00:02:45.159
1950s.

00:02:45.159 --> 00:02:48.929
So this is my family.

00:02:48.949 --> 00:02:49.949
Things normalized.

00:02:49.949 --> 00:02:55.699
I was born in 1964, so I'm 45 years old, and I grew up in a

00:02:55.719 --> 00:02:56.949
university

00:02:56.969 --> 00:02:59.719
community in the south side of Chicago and I basically was

00:02:59.409 --> 00:03:00.409
just a

00:03:00.409 --> 00:03:03.179
regular American kid.

00:03:03.199 --> 00:03:08.709
And when I became a teenager, as often happens in American

00:03:08.729 --> 00:03:10.469
families, I

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:13.189
decided to rebel against my family.

00:03:13.209 --> 00:03:15.479
How do you rebel against a family of Communists?

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:15.699
&gt;&gt;

00:03:15.699 --> 00:03:16.699
[Laughing]

00:03:15.699 --> 00:03:19.629
BILL B.: Well, I'll tell you how I rebelled.

00:03:19.649 --> 00:03:22.399
I put on a suit and tie and became a businessman.

00:03:22.149 --> 00:03:25.399
There's nothing else I could do the piss off my parents more

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:25.340
than

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:26.340
that.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:25.789
&gt;&gt;

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:26.590
[Laughing]

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:28.459
BILL B.: And I came to Stanford Business School.

00:03:28.479 --> 00:03:33.479
And so I sat in these rooms for two years, as many of you do

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.500
and will

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:39.079
be doing and have done, and I went to brown bag lunches and

00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:40.099
I went to

00:03:40.099 --> 00:03:42.849
recruiting events trying to figure out what I was gonna do

00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:43.659
with my

00:03:43.659 --> 00:03:44.659
life.

00:03:43.909 --> 00:03:46.659
And something didn't quite feel right because even though I

00:03:46.119 --> 00:03:47.119
was

00:03:47.119 --> 00:03:49.619
rebelling against my family to become a businessman, I just

00:03:49.219 --> 00:03:50.219
didn't

00:03:50.219 --> 00:03:52.179
quite feel right.

00:03:52.199 --> 00:03:55.699
And so as I was searching my soul to say what should I would

00:03:54.459 --> 00:03:55.459
do with

00:03:55.459 --> 00:03:56.459
my life?

00:03:55.959 --> 00:03:59.689
I said, what's my unique comparative advantage with all

00:03:59.709 --> 00:04:00.709
these other

00:04:00.709 --> 00:04:03.959
people that are all so smart, and all so good, and all so

00:04:03.349 --> 00:04:04.349
ambitious?

00:04:04.349 --> 00:04:07.599
And I thought, well, I'm a businessman but I am also the

00:04:07.199 --> 00:04:08.199
grandson of

00:04:08.199 --> 00:04:09.699
the head of the Communist Party.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:09.159
&gt;&gt;

00:04:09.159 --> 00:04:10.159
[Laughing]

00:04:09.159 --> 00:04:12.109
BILL B.: That's my competitive advantage.

00:04:12.129 --> 00:04:12.329
&gt;&gt;

00:04:12.329 --> 00:04:13.329
[Laughing]

00:04:12.329 --> 00:04:17.100
BILL B.: And it just so happened that 1989 was the year the

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.120
Berlin

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.610
Wall came down.

00:04:19.629 --> 00:04:24.110
And so I had a chance to do a business in the former

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:25.129
Communist

00:04:25.129 --> 00:04:26.129
countries.

00:04:25.879 --> 00:04:26.879
And guess what?

00:04:26.349 --> 00:04:29.349
Not a single person I knew anywhere in the world had any

00:04:28.439 --> 00:04:29.439
interest in

00:04:29.439 --> 00:04:30.439
doing it.

00:04:30.439 --> 00:04:33.689
And so I showed up, I started looking for jobs where I could

00:04:33.219 --> 00:04:34.219
be doing

00:04:34.219 --> 00:04:35.350
business in eastern Europe.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.370
Everyone said, why would you wanna do that?

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.540
There's no business in eastern Europe.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.810
And I looked for jobs and looked for jobs.

00:04:40.949 --> 00:04:43.699
People offered me all sorts of mainstream, normal jobs but I

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:43.949
wanted to

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:45.319
do business in eastern Europe.

00:04:45.339 --> 00:04:48.339
And eventually a got a job in the Boston Consulting Group in

00:04:47.509 --> 00:04:48.509
London.

00:04:48.509 --> 00:04:51.379
And they had an excentric partner there who said that, well,

00:04:51.399 --> 00:04:52.399
we don't

00:04:52.399 --> 00:04:55.399
have any business in eastern Europe but if we ever do, you

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.050
can be our

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:56.050
guy.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:59.970
You can be the head of our eastern European practice.

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:00.189
&gt;&gt;

00:05:00.189 --> 00:05:01.189
[Laughing]

00:05:00.189 --> 00:05:01.689
BILL B.: So I said, okay.

00:05:01.689 --> 00:05:03.939
That's as good as I'm gonna get.

00:05:03.439 --> 00:05:06.439
So, I went to London, I went to work at the Boston

00:05:05.939 --> 00:05:06.939
Consulting Group,

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:10.360
and indeed a few months later we got a first nibble of work

00:05:10.379 --> 00:05:11.379
in eastern

00:05:11.379 --> 00:05:12.389
Europe.

00:05:12.409 --> 00:05:17.439
And the work we got was with a bus factory in Poland in the

00:05:17.459 --> 00:05:18.459
southeast

00:05:18.459 --> 00:05:21.459
corner of Poland about six hours from Warsaw by car on the

00:05:20.599 --> 00:05:21.599
Ukrainian

00:05:21.599 --> 00:05:22.599
border.

00:05:21.919 --> 00:05:25.230
The bus factory was being -- almost going out of business.

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:28.000
I think their sales had declined by 90 percent and somehow

00:05:27.689 --> 00:05:28.689
the World

00:05:28.689 --> 00:05:32.350
Bank got involved can said, we need a consultant up here.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:35.620
And BCG put in a big proposal that said we have experts in

00:05:34.899 --> 00:05:35.899
buses and

00:05:35.899 --> 00:05:38.399
we have experts in manufacturing we have experts in all

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:38.740
these

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:39.740
different things.

00:05:39.319 --> 00:05:41.480
And the World Bank said great, send 'em.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:44.750
And so they sent me, as a first-year associate, fresh out of

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:44.370
Stanford.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:44.569
&gt;&gt;

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:45.370
[Laughing]

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:52.639
BILL B.: So I go to this failing bus factory and it's pretty

00:05:52.659 --> 00:05:53.659
clear

00:05:53.659 --> 00:05:56.149
that there's no hope for this bus factory.

00:05:56.169 --> 00:05:57.919
Their sales have declined by 90 percent.

00:05:57.899 --> 00:06:00.899
They're just gonna have to lay off 90 percent of their

00:06:00.149 --> 00:06:01.149
employees if

00:06:01.149 --> 00:06:02.399
they wanna stay in business.

00:06:02.399 --> 00:06:05.439
And so it was not a very pleasurable assignment.

00:06:05.459 --> 00:06:08.459
But one thing happened to me while I was sitting in this

00:06:07.339 --> 00:06:08.339
little town

00:06:08.339 --> 00:06:10.180
six hours from Warsaw.

00:06:10.199 --> 00:06:13.199
And I notice that in the newspaper one day they had all

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.060
these

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.180
financial statements in the middle of the newspaper.

00:06:16.199 --> 00:06:19.449
And I asked my translator -- I didn't speak a word of Polish

00:06:18.449 --> 00:06:19.449
-- I

00:06:19.449 --> 00:06:21.949
said, what are these financial statements? And he said, oh,

00:06:21.449 --> 00:06:22.449
these are

00:06:22.449 --> 00:06:24.699
the first privatizations of the Polish government's doing.

00:06:24.409 --> 00:06:25.909
I said, oh, that's interesting.

00:06:25.459 --> 00:06:25.659
&gt;&gt;

00:06:25.659 --> 00:06:26.659
[Laughing]

00:06:25.659 --> 00:06:29.480
BILL B.: I said, what does this thing say in what does this

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:30.500
thing

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:31.500
say?

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:33.500
And so we started to write down the numbers and basically

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.000
they were

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:38.339
selling seven Polish companies at valuations which were half

00:06:38.359 --> 00:06:39.359
of their

00:06:39.359 --> 00:06:40.980
one-year previous earnings.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:41.199
&gt;&gt;

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.000
[Laughing]

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:45.709
BILL B.: Okay, now, I wasn't actually all that great a

00:06:45.729 --> 00:06:46.729
student at

00:06:46.729 --> 00:06:50.589
Stanford but even not being a great student I understood

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:51.609
that if you

00:06:51.609 --> 00:06:55.109
buy a company at half of one year's earnings that's got to

00:06:54.319 --> 00:06:55.319
make sense;

00:06:55.319 --> 00:06:56.319
right?

00:06:55.569 --> 00:06:55.769
&gt;&gt;

00:06:55.569 --> 00:06:56.569
[Laughing]

00:06:55.569 --> 00:07:01.339
BILL B.: And I didn't have a lot of money.

00:07:01.359 --> 00:07:04.609
I don't come from a wealthy company or anything but I had

00:07:03.859 --> 00:07:04.859
saved up

00:07:04.859 --> 00:07:08.109
4,000 bucks at that point and I took my entire life savings

00:07:07.609 --> 00:07:08.609
which was

00:07:08.609 --> 00:07:11.859
4,000 bucks, I converted it to Polish zloty, I took it down,

00:07:11.359 --> 00:07:12.359
and I

00:07:12.359 --> 00:07:14.609
applied for shares in these first privatizations and I

00:07:14.109 --> 00:07:15.109
bought 'em.

00:07:15.109 --> 00:07:17.859
And they went up ten times over the next 12 months.

00:07:17.859 --> 00:07:20.859
Now, if you've ever made ten times your money on anything

00:07:20.629 --> 00:07:21.629
you'll know

00:07:21.629 --> 00:07:23.879
that it releases a certain chemical in your body.

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:23.879
&gt;&gt;

00:07:23.879 --> 00:07:24.879
[Laughing]

00:07:23.879 --> 00:07:36.490
BILL B.: And you want that chemical release again.

00:07:36.509 --> 00:07:36.709
&gt;&gt;

00:07:36.709 --> 00:07:37.709
[Laughing]

00:07:36.709 --> 00:07:40.209
BILL B.: And so I knew I had found my vocation. I was gonna

00:07:39.709 --> 00:07:40.709
go and

00:07:40.709 --> 00:07:42.800
buy into privatizations in eastern Europe.

00:07:42.819 --> 00:07:46.069
So we fast forward a couple years and I end up at Salomon

00:07:45.829 --> 00:07:47.029
Brothers.

00:07:47.049 --> 00:07:50.649
And I'm -- I got a job at Salomon Brotherss as an investment

00:07:50.669 --> 00:07:51.889
banker.

00:07:51.909 --> 00:07:54.909
So I go to work at Salomon Brothers as an investment banker

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:54.639
and

00:07:54.639 --> 00:07:56.139
Salomon Brothers doesn't exist anymore.

00:07:55.899 --> 00:07:58.899
It became part of City Group and City Group hardly exists or

00:07:58.089 --> 00:07:59.089
won't

00:07:59.089 --> 00:08:01.769
exist or whatever.

00:08:01.789 --> 00:08:05.039
And I go to work at Salomon Brothers and for those of you

00:08:04.259 --> 00:08:05.259
who have

00:08:05.259 --> 00:08:08.509
ever read "Liar's Poker", it's a great book and if you

00:08:07.509 --> 00:08:08.509
haven't, you

00:08:08.509 --> 00:08:09.509
you should.

00:08:09.009 --> 00:08:11.259
And it talks about the incredible culture of Salomon

00:08:10.759 --> 00:08:11.759
Brothers which

00:08:11.759 --> 00:08:13.670
was this dog-eat-dog place.

00:08:13.689 --> 00:08:17.189
And I go to work at Salomon Brothers and on my first day at

00:08:16.089 --> 00:08:17.089
Salomon

00:08:17.089 --> 00:08:19.339
Brothers as an investment banker for eastern Europe, they

00:08:18.759 --> 00:08:19.759
give me my

00:08:19.759 --> 00:08:22.509
business cards, they give me my desk, and they say, you

00:08:22.439 --> 00:08:23.439
basically have

00:08:23.439 --> 00:08:26.439
to earn five times what we're paying you otherwise you're

00:08:25.439 --> 00:08:26.439
gonna get

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:27.439
fired.

00:08:26.689 --> 00:08:27.990
Earn it for the firm.

00:08:28.009 --> 00:08:29.680
Get to work.

00:08:29.699 --> 00:08:34.129
So I -- there's no training program, there's no mentors,

00:08:34.149 --> 00:08:35.230
there's no

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:37.000
here's what you need to do.

00:08:36.189 --> 00:08:37.189
Get to work.

00:08:37.189 --> 00:08:40.250
Five times what we're paying you otherwise you get fired.

00:08:40.269 --> 00:08:43.419
So I hear that there's a privatization of the Hungarian

00:08:43.439 --> 00:08:45.289
Airline and

00:08:45.309 --> 00:08:47.059
there's some team working on it.

00:08:46.709 --> 00:08:50.490
And so I go to the conference room where they're supposed to

00:08:50.509 --> 00:08:51.509
be having

00:08:51.509 --> 00:08:55.159
a team meeting and I walk in and they say, what are you

00:08:55.179 --> 00:08:56.179
doing here?

00:08:56.179 --> 00:08:58.179
I said, well, I'm here to help.

00:08:57.929 --> 00:09:00.179
And they say, we don't need your help.

00:08:59.929 --> 00:09:01.429
This is well taken care of.

00:09:01.159 --> 00:09:02.159
Please leave.

00:09:02.159 --> 00:09:05.159
Because they didn't wanna share any of their five times with

00:09:04.009 --> 00:09:05.009
me

00:09:05.009 --> 00:09:07.509
because that was just gonna make their life more difficult.

00:09:07.509 --> 00:09:08.889
So no Hungary.

00:09:08.909 --> 00:09:12.259
I then heard about a Polish telecom privatization going on a

00:09:12.279 --> 00:09:13.279
couple

00:09:13.279 --> 00:09:16.779
days later and so I go ask try to wedge my way into that.

00:09:16.779 --> 00:09:19.779
And they say, don't etch think about trying to come anywhere

00:09:18.779 --> 00:09:19.779
near

00:09:19.779 --> 00:09:20.779
Poland.

00:09:20.029 --> 00:09:20.230
&gt;&gt;

00:09:20.029 --> 00:09:21.029
[Laughing]

00:09:20.029 --> 00:09:23.279
BILL B.: And I'm thinking, how am I ever gonna survive in

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:23.610
this firm?

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:25.610
They're extremely uncollegial.

00:09:25.629 --> 00:09:28.480
How am I ever gonna survive in this firm?

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.509
And then I came up with this idea.

00:09:30.529 --> 00:09:33.819
At the time, this was 1992, there was no investment banking

00:09:33.839 --> 00:09:34.839
work in

00:09:34.839 --> 00:09:35.839
Russia.

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:39.220
And so none of these guys were trying to protect their turf.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.740
And so I just declared myself the investment banker in

00:09:40.909 --> 00:09:41.909
charge of

00:09:41.909 --> 00:09:45.139
Russia because nobody --

00:09:45.159 --> 00:09:45.360
&gt;&gt;

00:09:45.159 --> 00:09:46.159
[Laughing]

00:09:45.159 --> 00:09:47.659
BILL B.: -- nobody was -- and there was nobody -- and I

00:09:47.159 --> 00:09:48.159
declared it

00:09:48.159 --> 00:09:50.409
waiting for somebody to object but nobody objected because

00:09:49.909 --> 00:09:50.909
there was

00:09:50.909 --> 00:09:51.909
no money.

00:09:51.409 --> 00:09:54.569
There was just nothing going on.

00:09:54.589 --> 00:09:56.939
Then I had an interesting opportunity about three months

00:09:56.959 --> 00:09:57.959
into my

00:09:57.959 --> 00:10:00.929
