00:12:52.269 --> 00:12:53.269
visitors and I

00:12:53.269 --> 00:12:55.769
just started circling people in the Yellow Page directly and

00:12:55.039 --> 00:12:56.039
going

00:12:56.039 --> 00:12:57.039
around meeting them.

00:12:56.789 --> 00:13:00.289
And I met about 30 people and over the course of a week I

00:12:59.789 --> 00:13:00.789
put together

00:13:00.789 --> 00:13:04.460
the sort of thought about what this is.

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:05.759
And it was very simple.

00:13:05.779 --> 00:13:09.679
That they had vouchers that they gave to every person in the

00:13:09.699 --> 00:13:10.699
country

00:13:10.699 --> 00:13:13.449
and there was a hundred 150 million people in the country

00:13:12.949 --> 00:13:13.949
and each

00:13:13.949 --> 00:13:15.500
voucher costs 20 bucks.

00:13:15.519 --> 00:13:19.699
So that gave you $3 billion worth of vouchers and that was

00:13:19.719 --> 00:13:22.469
exchangeable for 30 percent of all the shared capital of all

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:22.740
the

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:25.490
shares in Russia which meant the entire value of Russia in

00:13:25.469 --> 00:13:27.129
1992 was

00:13:27.149 --> 00:13:29.269
$10 billion for the whole country.

00:13:29.289 --> 00:13:32.039
All the oil, all the gas, all the metals, all the

00:13:31.059 --> 00:13:32.059
everything.

00:13:32.059 --> 00:13:34.079
$10 billion.

00:13:34.099 --> 00:13:36.599
And, boy, at this point, the adrenaline is just pumping

00:13:35.629 --> 00:13:36.629
through my

00:13:36.629 --> 00:13:39.379
system and it was clear that this was just the most

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:40.230
unbelievable,

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:43.799
unbelievable opportunity ever.

00:13:43.819 --> 00:13:46.819
So, I go back to Salomon Brothers, where I had been working

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:47.730
and I say,

00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:50.730
listen, we're wasting our time with all this 50,000-dollar

00:13:49.529 --> 00:13:50.740
advisory

00:13:50.759 --> 00:13:51.759
stuff.

00:13:51.019 --> 00:13:54.019
We should get in there, buy all this stuff, and make a

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:53.860
fortune.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:55.360
They're just giving it away.

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:57.309
Gold for free.

00:13:57.329 --> 00:14:01.909
And they looked at me like I was completely out of my mind.

00:14:01.929 --> 00:14:04.529
And I thought, how could -- and people said, what?

00:14:04.549 --> 00:14:05.819
Russia? Invest in Russia?

00:14:05.839 --> 00:14:06.839
What are you?

00:14:06.589 --> 00:14:11.399
Crazy is this and I didn't know how to work in an

00:14:11.419 --> 00:14:12.419
organization, or

00:14:12.419 --> 00:14:13.419
politics, or anything.

00:14:13.169 --> 00:14:16.169
And so the more that they -- the more people sort of blanked

00:14:15.669 --> 00:14:16.669
me and

00:14:16.669 --> 00:14:19.919
didn't wanna talk about it the more I would just, like, try

00:14:19.169 --> 00:14:20.169
to find

00:14:20.169 --> 00:14:21.919
somebody else who would listen to me.

00:14:21.919 --> 00:14:25.169
Ask so I was just talking to more and more people which is

00:14:24.669 --> 00:14:25.669
exactly the

00:14:25.669 --> 00:14:28.419
wrong this I think to do in an organization that starts

00:14:27.919 --> 00:14:28.919
going on.

00:14:28.919 --> 00:14:31.669
And so pretty soon -- we used to have these group lunches

00:14:31.169 --> 00:14:32.169
with the

00:14:32.169 --> 00:14:34.919
young guys who are in the same year and people stopped

00:14:34.669 --> 00:14:35.669
inviting me to

00:14:35.669 --> 00:14:36.919
the group lunches, no more.

00:14:36.719 --> 00:14:36.919
&gt;&gt;

00:14:36.919 --> 00:14:37.919
[Laughing]

00:14:36.919 --> 00:14:38.169
BILL B.: No more drinks.

00:14:38.169 --> 00:14:40.169
People didn't wanna with seen with me.

00:14:39.919 --> 00:14:41.169
I was some excentric outcast.

00:14:41.169 --> 00:14:43.919
And I wasn't earning any money for the firm, either.

00:14:43.669 --> 00:14:46.169
That five times thing was coming close to being due.

00:14:46.169 --> 00:14:48.919
So I was in this terrible situation of becoming, like, an

00:14:48.419 --> 00:14:49.419
outcast in

00:14:49.419 --> 00:14:52.669
the firm, and very unpopular, and my job was on the line and

00:14:52.169 --> 00:14:53.169
I was

00:14:53.169 --> 00:14:54.419
feeling very bad about myself.

00:14:54.419 --> 00:14:57.919
And one day I got a call from a very senior person in the

00:14:57.419 --> 00:14:58.419
New York

00:14:58.419 --> 00:15:00.919
office who's responsible for the firm's balance sheet.

00:15:00.419 --> 00:15:02.919
And he said, I heard that you might have something

00:15:02.669 --> 00:15:03.669
interesting to say

00:15:03.669 --> 00:15:04.669
about Russia.

00:15:04.169 --> 00:15:06.669
Why don't you come and tell me about it?

00:15:06.419 --> 00:15:10.340
And so I prepare myself a PowerPoint presentation so

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:11.360
hopefully I can

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:13.860
somehow get through to this guy and maybe turn this

00:15:13.689 --> 00:15:14.689
situation around.

00:15:14.689 --> 00:15:18.850
Can so I go with New York and this guy is meeting with this

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:19.870
very, very

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:24.269
strange fellow with no social graces whatsoever and he was,

00:15:24.289 --> 00:15:25.289
like, one

00:15:25.289 --> 00:15:28.840
of their most successful investors in the firm but nobody

